{
  "decision": "D8",
  "description": "Display names (name.fr / name.en) for arrondissements whose OCHA COD-AB name dropped accents or an apostrophe. Only diacritics and apostrophes change: every display name folds (normalizeName) to the OCHA name. Numbered arrondissements get Roman numerals by rule in scripts/generate.ts, not here. OCHA's form stays in refName and aliases.",
  "rule": "Evidence order: signed decree (2007/115, 2010/198) > other official source (MINFI 2019, BUCREP 2005, ELECAM 2025) > established usage (OSM / geoBoundaries, French-language usage). A decree that prints the plain form in mixed case overrides weaker evidence (see notRestored). MINFI drops accents almost everywhere, so its plain forms are not counted against an accent. Capital initials stay unaccented, as in official usage (Ebolowa, Edéa, Eséka).",
